          <TD>
            <P class=text align=justify>The Royal Thai Embassy is pleased to 
            announce the opening of the VFS Thailand Visa Application Centre in 
            New Delhi. Indian residents who wish to apply for Transit Visas, 
            Tourist Visas or Non-Immigrant Visas can now submit their 
            applications at the new application centre. <BR><BR>Applications 
            submitted in the Delhi application centre will be assessed by the 
            Royal Thai Embassy, New Delhi. <BR><BR>We offer the option of 
            courier service for return of passport, directly at your doorstep. 
            <BR><BR>All relevant information pertaining to Thai visa is 
            available on this site. Please read the information carefully to 
            expedite the processing of your application. <BR><BR>If you have 
            already applied for a Thailand Visa at the new application centre, 
            you can now also <A 
            href="http://www.vfs-thailand.co.in/trackyourapplication.html"><BR>Track 
            your Application</A> using our advanced Visa Application Tracking 
            System. <BR><BR><B>Important Notices</B><BR><BR>In the month of 
            August, The Royal Thai Embassy will be closed for official holidays 
            on Friday 12 August 2005 (HM The Queen's Birthday) &amp; Monday, 15 
            2005 (Independence Day of India)<BR><BR>Effectively, applications 
            submitted in </P>
            <UL>
              <LI><SPAN class=text>Session 1 (08.00-10.00 hrs) of Thurs. 11 Aug 
              05 will be returned on Tuesday 16 Aug05 </SPAN>
              <LI><SPAN class=text>Session 2 (12.00 -16.00 hrs) of Thurs. 11 Aug 
              05 will be returned on Wednesday 17 Aug05 </SPAN></LI></UL>
            <P><A class=text 
            href="http://www.vfs-thailand.co.in/importantnotices.html"><B>Important 
            Notices</B></A> </P><BR></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>
